          "children": [
            {
              "type": "note",
              "id": "umUsf",
              "name": "Note Pane",
              "width": 352,
              "height": 468,
              "content": "ESTIMATE PANE\nRight pane at width >= 1200: pinned, does not scroll with the form. Unit lines are read-only (name + subtotal, 'Belum dipilih' for an empty unit); the rail is the only unit switcher. Total + duration update live, 150 ms crossfade; MediaQuery.disableAnimations = instant. Numbers use tabular figures (FontFeature.tabularFigures) so the total does not shift while it updates. Lanjut follows the same gate as the sticky bar: enabled only when every chip is complete, else disabled with the reason line ('Pilih layanan untuk PCX 160' = first incomplete unit). No voucher here (starts at S16). Semantics: region 'Estimasi biaya'; the total is a polite live region."
            },
            {
              "type": "note",
              "id": "dhoHJ",
              "name": "Note Rail",
              "width": 352,
              "height": 426,
              "content": "UNIT RAIL\nWidth >= 840: chips become a rail (252 dp), pinned, form scrolls beside it. Same rows and states as the phone chips. Semantics: list 'Motor', row 'Beat 110, lengkap, dipilih'. Focus order: rail, form, pane (Lanjut is the last stop; with one unit: form, pane). Arrow up / down moves focus in the rail, Enter selects (keyboard / switch access), focus ring = 2 dp focus-ring. Switching keeps each unit's in-progress state, selection 150 ms. A long nickname wraps and the row grows (no fixed height). The completion badge stays in the wide stepper (centered 720)."
            },
            {
              "type": "note",
              "id": "QzMpT",
              "name": "Note Breakpoints",
              "width": 352,
              "height": 447,
              "content": "BREAKPOINTS + MODAL\n>= 1200: rail + form + pane (1 unit: form + pane, no rail). 840-1199: rail + form + sticky pill (width = form column). 600-839: chip row on top + form + pill (720). Rotating keeps the active unit, each unit's draft and scroll offset. Salin dari source sheet = centered 560 modal on tablet (focus trapped, Esc / scrim tap closes, focus returns to the Salin dari row; close X semantics 'Tutup'; source rows have the focused state in the Focus section); the destructive dialog is identical at every width. On-screen keyboard on tablet: the form scrolls, pane / rail stay put, the pill moves above the keyboard."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
